WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.475
A checklist matters because it puts every
habit in one place you can check quickly.

2
00:00:04.475 --> 00:00:08.152
This one follows the same
moments we've walked through:

3
00:00:08.152 --> 00:00:12.075
before the meeting, the start,
during it, the close, and after.

4
00:00:12.075 --> 00:00:16.607
Each row is a handful of quick checks, from
whether a meeting is needed at all, to

5
00:00:16.607 --> 00:00:18.377
the decision-maker attending,

6
00:00:18.377 --> 00:00:21.563
to the action items being
reviewed at the next meeting.

7
00:00:21.563 --> 00:00:23.737
It's the whole guide, on one page.

8
00:00:23.737 --> 00:00:27.410
For anyone who wants to go deeper,
two books are worth the time.
